OrionLayer open fix 102 — the galaxy map's merge-relocation mode on the wire
============================================================================

Work order 310 (Data, 19 October 2026: "Mach alles in einem Rutsch.";
309's finding 5). orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.0), on
top of open fix 101; commit f93344f6. Not on `orionlayer-local`. In
src/ext/ext_api.cpp, which is built only with ORION2RE_EXT.

F4 on the galaxy map turns MAINSCR::merging_relocations on and swaps the
pointer over the map to the relocation cursor (Check_Function_Keys_,
mainscr.cpp:3112-3129 in the 1.60 source; v2 :3326-3343); the next star
click that is no black hole sets every relocation to that star and says so
in HESTR 0xDD's box (mainscr_main.cpp:455-462; v2 :473-481); any negative
input clears the flag first (:396-399; v2 :417-420) — a right click on the
map, another F key, and F4 itself, whose case then sets it again. The flag
was on the wire nowhere: FLTS carries FLT1::merging_relocations, the Fleets
screen's own variable of the same name, and only while that screen is up.
So a client could not show the mode, and the next star click re-routed
every relocation without a sign.

The block: "MREL" on SCREEN_MAIN, after PLSM's place — a version byte (1),
then uint8 the flag (0 or 1). Read only.

commit f93344f66d13c68b36aa7552b76e95a6e192729c
Author: Data-crea <sattler.daniel@hotmail.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 19 12:49:35 2026 +0200

    OrionLayer Open Fix 102: the galaxy map's merge-relocation mode on the wire ("MREL" on SCREEN_MAIN after PLSM's place: a version byte and MAINSCR::merging_relocations, which F4 sets; FLTS carries only the Fleets screen's FLT1 flag of the same name)
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 11945b85..c1c63c1c 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -2350,6 +2350,30 @@ static void SerializeState(std::vector<uint8_t>& buf,
         Write8(buf, (uint8_t)MOX::g_ship_move_info.blackhole_blocks);
         Write8(buf, (uint8_t)MOX::g_ship_move_info.insufficient_fuel);
     }
+
+    // 34. The galaxy map's merge-relocation mode: "MREL", written ONLY on
+    //     SCREEN_MAIN, after PLSM's place. OrionLayer, open fix 102.
+    //
+    //     F4 (Check_Function_Keys, mainscr.cpp:3326-3343) turns
+    //     MAINSCR::merging_relocations on and swaps the pointer to the
+    //     relocation cursor over the map (mouse_list_relocation,
+    //     mainscr.cpp:192-195); the next star click then sets every
+    //     relocation to that star (mainscr_main.cpp:473-481), and any
+    //     negative input - a right click on the map, an F key, F4 itself,
+    //     whose case then sets it again - clears it first (:417-420). The
+    //     flag was on the wire nowhere: FLTS
+    //     carries the Fleets screen's own FLT1::merging_relocations, a
+    //     different variable, so a client could not show the mode. A
+    //     version byte, then the flag. Read only; nothing here changes the
+    //     game.
+    if (current_screen == SCREEN_MAIN) {
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'M');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'R');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'E');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'L');
+        Write8(buf, 1);                                   // block version
+        Write8(buf, MAINSCR::merging_relocations != 0 ? (uint8_t)1 : (uint8_t)0);
+    }
 }
 
